WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:04.880
Well he would treat people, you know.

2
00:00:04.880 --> 00:00:06.188
I don't know with something.

3
00:00:06.188 --> 00:00:12.880
Later on . . . I remember it real well because I would go bring her medicine.

4
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:21.120
He would go in the woods, and he . . . I should know how to do it because I boiled the tea for him.

5
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:23.180
He had a big black pot.

6
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:28.140
He would go in the woods, I'd go with him, and he would get different things.

7
00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:39.560
Some plants, they are flowers in the yard . . . some by the yard, and they make like a fan, the leaf.

8
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:42.940
I remember him putting that in that water.

9
00:00:42.940 --> 00:00:47.560
And he sure would heal people, and they would get well.

10
00:00:47.560 --> 00:00:49.560
But I don't remember the rest.

11
00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:50.480
So he was a healer?

12
00:00:50.480 --> 00:00:56.020
[Agrees] And he would let some whiskey, too.

13
00:00:56.020 --> 00:00:58.320
And he would sell it.

14
00:00:58.320 --> 00:00:59.820
He made whiskey?

15
00:00:59.820 --> 00:01:00.912
Yeah, with some corn.

16
00:01:00.912 --> 00:01:03.040
I'd help him.

17
00:01:03.040 --> 00:01:09.380
Anything he had to do, he'd always make me help him because I was the tallest one . . . the oldest one.

18
00:01:09.380 --> 00:01:12.040
And I never taste the whiskey.

19
00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:15.780
I work with my daddy and I never taste the whiskey.

20
00:01:15.780 --> 00:01:25.120
My sister next to me, she would drink [beeping noise] when my daddy didn't see her.

21
00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:26.420
One day she got drunk.

22
00:01:26.420 --> 00:01:29.240
Real little.

23
00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:31.607
When she got better my daddy whipped her.

24
00:01:31.607 --> 00:01:35.520
But to taste that whiskey.

25
00:01:35.520 --> 00:01:38.160
And you would sell the liquor.

26
00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.680
He made beer, too.

27
00:01:40.680 --> 00:01:43.460
Make tea for the one that was sick.
